[{"text":"TensorFunction[t, mu, nu, ...] transform into t[LorentzIndex[mu], LorentzIndex[nu], ...], i.e., it can be used as an unspecified tensorial function t.","anchor":"tensorfunction"},{"text":"A symmetric tensor can be obtained by TensorFunction[{t, \"S\"}, mu, nu, ...], and an antisymmetric one by TensorFunction[{t, \"A\"}, mu, nu, ...].","anchor":"tensorfunction"},{"text":"Overview, FCSymmetrize, FCAntiSymmetrize.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"TensorFunction[t, \\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Tau]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[t(\\mu ,\\nu ,\\tau )\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"TensorFunction[t, \\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Tau]] // StandardForm (*t[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Tau]]]*)","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Contract[FV[p, \\[Mu]] TensorFunction[t, \\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Tau]]]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[t\\left(\\overline{p},\\nu ,\\tau \\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Contract[FV[p, \\[Mu]] TensorFunction[t, \\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Tau]]] // StandardForm (*t[Momentum[p], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Tau]]]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"TensorFunction[{f, \"S\"}, \\[Alpha], \\[Beta]]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[f(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"TensorFunction[{f, \"S\"}, \\[Beta], \\[Alpha]] // StandardForm (*f[LorentzIndex[\\[Alpha]], LorentzIndex[\\[Beta]]]*)","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Attributes[f] ClearAttributes[f, Orderless]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{\\text{Orderless}\\}\\]","anchor":"cb7-2","section":"Examples"}]